From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:31:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm-vma-drop-mm-asynchronously-in-vma_start_read-fix

tweak comment, per Lorenzo

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/awXHR007d8MlhJUC@gremlin
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Cc: "Lorenzo Stoakes (ARM)" <ljs@kernel.org>

 mm/mmap_lock.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
---
 mm/mmap_lock.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/mmap_lock.c b/mm/mmap_lock.c
index 6e964a9aad70e..22132f87e90fe 100644
--- a/mm/mmap_lock.c
+++ b/mm/mmap_lock.c
@@ -300,7 +300,7 @@ static struct vm_area_struct *vma_start_read(struct mm_struct *mm,
 err_unstable:
 	/*
 	 * If vma got attached to another mm from under us, that mm is not
-	 * stable and can be freed in the narrow window after vma->vm_refcnt
+	 * stable and can be reused in the narrow window after vma->vm_refcnt
 	 * is dropped and before rcuwait_wake_up(mm) is called. Grab it before
 	 * releasing vma->vm_refcnt.
 	 */
-- 
2.47.3

